# gstack Embedded Rules

## Logging
- Use ESP_LOGI / ESP_LOGW / ESP_LOGE with a static const char* TAG.
- Never use printf for runtime output.

## Error handling
- Wrap all ESP-IDF SDK calls with ESP_ERROR_CHECK() unless the error is
  explicitly handled (log + propagate esp_err_t, or documented fallback).

## RTOS synchronisation
- Prefer FreeRTOS Task Notifications (xTaskNotify / ulTaskNotifyTake) over
  binary semaphores for single-consumer event signalling — lower overhead,
  no dynamic allocation.
- Use semaphores / mutexes only when multiple producers or shared resources
  require it; document the reason in a comment.

## Architecture
- Every hardware peripheral or logical subsystem lives in components/<name>/.
- Each component exposes a public API only through include/<name>.h.
- main/ depends on components via REQUIRES / PRIV_REQUIRES in CMakeLists.txt.
- Never reach into another component's .c files directly.
- One FreeRTOS task owns the I2C bus; never call I2C from an ISR or BLE callback.

## High-velocity delivery
- When implementing any new feature, supply all three:
    1. Header:  include/<name>.h   — public API + Doxygen comments
    2. Implementation: <name>.c    — gstack error + logging patterns
    3. Usage:   main.c snippet     — minimal call site example
